  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 200 PM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\n- Dry and Warmer through Wednesday\n\nA stretch of nice weather is expected as high pressure builds into\nthe area. We'll be stuck in a pattern where an upper level ridge\nis over the eastern CONUS and a trough over the western CONUS.\nDuring this time we should see mostly sunny to partly cloudy skies\nand temperatures warming each day as low to mid level temperatures\nrise. Highs the next few days will be in the 50s with lows in the\nmid 20s to low 30s tonight warming into low to mid 30s the next\nfew nights (warmer near the lake).\n\n- Chance of Rain Thursday and Saturday/Sunday, Mild\n\nThe ridge axis shifts east a little bringing southwest flow to the\narea and warm air advection. This will allow for a couple\nshortwave troughs to swing through Thursday and over the weekend.\nThursday's wave is largely north of the area and could keep rain\nchances (20 percent) to the north as well. A deeper trough shown\nin the ensembles moves through over the weekend, but there is low\nconfidence in the exact timing. \n\nWinds could be breezy with each system with the potential for 40\nmph gusts along the lakeshore this weekend. Temperatures are\nexpected to be in the mid 50s to mid 60s with lows in the 40s.",
